tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:1:20:error:CleanProse.NoForceWords:§2: 'try to' states no force. Write a force word, or a Conditional sentence if the force is conditional.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:4:1:error:CleanProse.NoForceWords:§2: 'It is a good idea to' states no force. Write a force word, or a Conditional sentence if the force is conditional.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:4:1:suggestion:CleanProse.VagueAntecedent:§1: 'It is' opens on a bare pronoun. Name the noun unless it is the previous sentence's subject. If the sentence only justifies the one before it, cut it per §7 unless §8 keeps the reason.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:7:1:warning:CleanProse.ThroatClearing:§7: 'This section explains' announces text instead of stating a rule. Cut it.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:10:5:suggestion:CleanProse.LowercaseForce:§2: 'need to' is outside the force vocabulary. If it states obligation, permission, or preference, write the force word (MUST, NEVER, SHOULD, MAY, PREFER X OVER Y). If it does not, leave it.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:13:27:suggestion:CleanProse.VagueAntecedent:§1: 'This keeps' opens on a bare pronoun. Name the noun unless it is the previous sentence's subject. If the sentence only justifies the one before it, cut it per §7 unless §8 keeps the reason.
tests/clean-prose/Wrapped.md:16:1:suggestion:CleanProse.ConditionLast:§1: the condition follows the action. Write 'If C, do X', not 'Do X if C'.
